{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgvyqT8XpkzHHZLNFG6xX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Egy2wxhxkG36dQr3yfTVNV","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /workspace/paper; python3 - <<'E'\np=open('paper.tex').read()\na=\"A method that works for models resembling the sources may degrade exactly where evaluation savings matter most, namely when comparing new, stronger systems.\"\nassert a in p\np=p.replace(a,\"A method that works for models resembling the sources may degrade exactly where evaluation savings matter most, namely when comparing new, stronger systems. Predicting the behaviour of more capable models from results on weaker ones is a recognized and difficult target elsewhere in language-model evaluation---observational scaling laws, for example, fit capability measures on existing models and extrapolate to more capable ones \\\\citep{Ruan2024ObservationalSL}---but we are not aware of a grounded measurement of how few-item benchmark prediction behaves out of range, which is the gap we probe here.\")\nb=\"The latent model is an IRT-style logistic model \\\\citep{Rodriguez2021EvaluationEA} fitted to a model-by-item matrix.\"\nassert b in p\np=p.replace(b,\"The latent model is an IRT-style logistic model \\\\citep{Rodriguez2021EvaluationEA} fitted to a model-by-item matrix; with a vector of abilities per model and item-specific loadings it is a compensatory multidimensional IRT model, whose item information and ability estimation are treated in \\\\citet{Reckase2009MultidimensionalIR}, and the item-information criterion we use for selection is the same quantity that drives item selection in adaptive testing \\\\citep{Zhuang2023PositionAE}.\")\nc=\"The final estimator follows the model-assisted approach of correcting a model-based prediction with an observed-sample residual, in the spirit of prediction-powered inference \\\\citep{Angelopoulos2023PredictionpoweredI}.\"\nassert c in p\np=p.replace(c,\"The final estimator follows the model-assisted approach of survey sampling, which corrects a model-based prediction with the mean residual of an observed sample, and which has been extended to flexible machine-learned predictors \\\\citep{Breidt2017ModelAssistedSE}; prediction-powered inference \\\\citep{Angelopoulos2023PredictionpoweredI} is a recent descendant of the same idea.\")\nopen('paper.tex','w').write(p)\nE\npython3 - <<'E'\nimport json\nc=json.load(open('/workspace/paper/claims_grounding.json'))\nprint(json.dumps(c['claims'][-2:],indent=1)); print([x['claim'][:60] for x in c['claims']][:40])\nE\ngrep -o '\"id\": \"ref[^\"]*\"' references_provenance.json | tail -3; grep -n \"^ref\\|ref\\.\" claims_grounding.json | head -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1052,"cache_read_input_tokens":75476,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1052},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"df23ce4c-1fc4-46ff-ab9f-e2ced463f1d4","uuid":"a65c2d3d-39b0-48ea-a96a-eedb29409119","timestamp":"2026-11-11T10:26:48.987Z","request_id":"req_011CgvyqSbnZWkZrtTZG4wmT"}
