I rewrote the three flagged paragraphs of `paper.tex` with new citations. The paper compiles to 13 pages with no LaTeX errors or undefined citations. No numbers changed.

- **References:** Semantic Scholar rate-limited me (HTTP 429) and the earlier retrieval had stopped without adding anything. I looked up three references on OpenAlex instead, and the bibliography is now at the 30-entry cap. I confirmed the title, authors and venue from OpenAlex records.
  - Ruan et al., NeurIPS 2024, on observational scaling laws.
  - Breidt & Opsomer, *Statistical Science* 2017, on model-assisted survey estimation with modern prediction techniques.
  - Reckase, *Multidimensional Item Response Theory*, Springer 2009. I found this one only through OpenAlex book-review records, not a direct entry, so check its details.
- **Introduction (strong-target motivation):** it now places out-of-range prediction alongside observational scaling laws, and says the few-item benchmark case is not settled by those results. I left out any claim about what Zhang et al. found, because the artifacts only support using their data.
- **Related work, IRT and Fisher design:** it now describes the model as compensatory multidimensional IRT and links its item information to adaptive-testing item selection.
- **Related work, model-assisted estimator:** it now frames the estimator as the survey-sampling approach, extended to machine-learned predictors, with prediction-powered inference as a recent descendant.
- **Unrelated fix:** the GPQA bib title had an unescaped `&`, which caused a LaTeX error. I escaped it.
- **Grounding and checks:**
